  "implementation": [
    "Intrinsic flex-basis reuses native Size parsing and existing preferred-size conversion.",
    "z-index math reuses native CSSNumber parsing, rounds ties toward positive infinity, and saturates at the engine integer bounds. Literal fractions stay invalid; non-finite results remain outside the new path.",
    "Native selector AST validation covers retained Has constraints, known functional pseudo names/arguments and picker identifiers, including uppercase SELECT. Forgiving :is/:where lists retain their existing behavior.",
    "Existing counter argument/list consumers are shared by syntax checking and renderer conversion. Custom styles remain syntactically distinct from rendering support. Empty attr() is rejected; the full modern attr grammar is not implemented.",
    "Native fallback and supported generated-content/counter eligibility are cached at stylesheet preparation. Value conversions remain in their property-family handlers; unsupported generated images retain the previous fallback."
  ],
  "initial_issues_corrected": [
    "An uppercase SELECT regression found by the full WPT audit was corrected.",
    "An existing allocation test found five unnecessary allocations when rejecting a string counter-style argument. A primitive-token guard removed them.",
    "First timing run showed about 3% synthetic cascade slowdown. Follow-up work removed unrelated custom-property lookup work and moved native conversions out of the central application path. Final paired measurements are recorded separately.",
    "The feature-heavy comparison exposed repeated content/counter eligibility validation per styled element. Supported declarations now cache this decision during preparation."
  ],
